        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(discord): guard message handler against malformed gateway dispatch data",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Discord message handler in `extensions/discord/src/monitor/message-handler.ts` accesses `entry.data` properties without optional chaining, risking crashes at runtime when the gateway dispatches malformed or incomplete data.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nA defensive programming audit identified 4 locations in the message handler where `entry.data` or `last.data` are accessed without null safety:\n\n1. **`buildKey` callback**: `entry.data.message` and `entry.data.channel_id` are accessed without accounting for `entry.data` being undefined.\n2. **`onFlush` combined text builder**: `entry.data.message` in a `.map()` callback — any single entry with missing data crashes the entire flush.\n3. **`onFlush` synthetic message**: `last.data.message` is used as argument to `Object.create`/`Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptors` — both throw on null/undefined.\n\n## User Impact\n\nWithout these guards, a single malformed gateway dispatch event can crash the entire Discord message processing pipeline, causing message loss and requiring a gateway restart.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Fix summary (4 guards added)\n\n| Location | Change | Protection |\n|----------|--------|-----------|\n| `buildKey` entry.data access | `entry.data.message` → `entry.data?.message` | Graceful skip of malformed entries |\n| `buildKey` channel_id access | `entry.data.channel_id` → `entry.data?.channel_id` | Graceful skip of entries without channel |\n| combined text builder | `entry.data.message` → guarded `entry.data?.message` | Null entries filtered out, not crashing |\n| synthetic message | Added `if (!last.data?.message) return` | Early return prevents `Object.create(null)` crash |\n\n### Tests\n\nAll 1825+ existing Discord extension tests pass (160 test files), including all `message-handler.*` preflight and bot-self-filter tests.",
        "branch": "fix/defensive-discord-optional-chaining",
